      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DHAULAGIRI NZ (7) had little luck fresh but atoned with a tough win at Mildura last week, getting home by a nose after taking control early in proceedings. Interesting to see what unfolds from this wide draw but he'll be fitter and his record at this circuit and distance stands at three wins and a placing from four attempts. With even luck he can get the job done again. LAST TANGO IN HEAVEN NZ (1) continued his consistent form when third last start, coming from wider to be beaten 4 metres. That was his fourth straight top-four result since recording back-to-back wins here. The ace draw could see him back in the winners' list. OUR INDIFFERENCE NZ (6) draws wider but is unbeaten at this circuit and distance and is hard to knock after saluting in good style last week, his fifth win in seven starts since switching from Queensland. HEZROCKINROYALTY (2) has trialled and gets a good draw for his return so keep safe.",
